  "text": {
    "id": {
      "title": "Binary search tree",
      "story": "Buat class `BST`. Setiap node punya nilai, anak kiri, dan anak kanan. Semua nilai di subtree kiri lebih kecil dari node itu, dan semua nilai di subtree kanan lebih besar.\nMetode: `insert(v)` (nilai yang sudah ada diabaikan), `contains(v)`, `min()` dan `max()` (`null` kalau tree kosong), `height()` (tree kosong 0, satu node 1), dan `inorder()` yang mengembalikan semua nilai sebagai array urut naik.",
      "hint1": "Untuk `insert` dan `contains`, mulai dari akar lalu belok kiri kalau nilainya lebih kecil, atau kanan kalau lebih besar.",
      "hint2": "`height` dan `inorder` paling mudah ditulis rekursif. Tinggi sebuah node adalah 1 ditambah tinggi anak yang paling tinggi."
    },
    "en": {
      "title": "Binary search tree",
      "story": "Build a `BST` class. Each node has a value, a left child, and a right child. Every value in the left subtree is smaller than the node, and every value in the right subtree is bigger.\nMethods: `insert(v)` (ignore values already in the tree), `contains(v)`, `min()` and `max()` (`null` for an empty tree), `height()` (0 for empty, 1 for a single node), and `inorder()` which returns all values as an ascending array.",
      "hint1": "For `insert` and `contains`, start at the root and go left when the value is smaller, right when it's bigger.",
      "hint2": "`height` and `inorder` are easiest as recursive functions. A node's height is 1 plus the height of its taller child."
    }
  },
